title: Zed Configuration
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The [[Zed|https://zed.dev]] editor can start a ~TiddlyWiki MCP (Model Context Protocol) server, which lets Zed's AI agent read and write the tiddlers of a wiki folder. The server is provided by the plugins `wikilabs/tw-mcp` and `wikilabs/tw-mcp-core` from https://github.com/wikilabs/plugins.

!! Prerequisites

* ~TiddlyWiki is installed globally, see [[Installation]]
* Both plugins are in a folder listed in the environment variable `TIDDLYWIKI_PLUGIN_PATH`, see [[Installation]]. Restart Zed after you change the variable

!! Configure the server

Create the file `.zed/settings.json` in the folder you open in Zed. Zed starts the server in that folder, so the wiki path is relative to it. The example serves the `tw5.com-server` edition of the ~TiddlyWiki5 repository:

```json
{
	"context_servers": {
		"tiddlywiki": {
			"command": "tiddlywiki",
			"args": [
				"+plugins/tiddlywiki/filesystem",
				"+plugins/wikilabs/tw-mcp-core",
				"+plugins/wikilabs/tw-mcp",
				"./editions/tw5.com-server",
				"--mcp",
				"readwrite",
				"label=zed-tw-mcp"
			]
		}
	}
}
```

; `+plugins/tiddlywiki/filesystem`
: Saves changes to tiddler files on disk. It must be loaded at startup
; `+plugins/wikilabs/tw-mcp-core`
: Required by `tw-mcp`, which does not load it by itself
; `+plugins/wikilabs/tw-mcp`
: Provides the `--mcp` command
; `./editions/tw5.com-server`
: The wiki folder
; `--mcp readwrite`
: Lets the agent change tiddlers. Without `readwrite` the server is read-only
; `label=zed-tw-mcp`
: A name that identifies the server in its log output and in `get_wiki_info`

To use the server in every project, add the entry to Zed's global settings file instead, with an absolute wiki path.

!! Start the server

# Open the folder in Zed
# Trust the folder when Zed asks. In Restricted Mode, Zed does not start servers defined in project settings
# Open the Agent panel and ask the agent to call `get_wiki_info`. The answer shows the label and `Filesystem: yes`

To restart the server, for example after you change a plugin, run `workspace: reload` from the command palette. It restarts Zed.

!! LSP

Completion and hovers in `.tid` files would need a small Zed extension, see [[LSP Editor Setup]].
